 "comment": "The short cross-check of the eight T1 nodes on one RTX 6000 Ada card of the Ada host (ucrtasl), as xc3: per node the default part (n_edits + 1 configurations x default, default_repeat = 10 runs) under the node's G.1b environment and harness pin, compared bit for bit with the node's sealed TASL-2 attempt (references). A PASS is what an addendum note lists to admit the node's G.5 audit chunks on an Ada card (g5_audit_hosts.check_admission) and what R1-HOST-FREE (2)(b) asks before a node's Ada results are used with its TASL floor; it does not by itself make the RTX 6000 Ada the table's hardware class (R1-HOST-FREE (2)(a); R1-G5-AUDIT-HOST-CLASS, proposed). The host's identity fields are filled from the compute agent's survey before a note can bind this spec; the G.1b census ran on RTX 6000 Ada cards, so the estimate ratio is 1.0.",
